{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "The Government should take 20% VAT on fuel but no duty",
        "additional_details": "The UK Government should cap fuel taxation using VAT at 20% but with no additional fuel duties or hidden taxes. In the USA, petrol can cost the equivalent of around 84p per litre, while British motorists here in the UK face much higher prices. For most people, fuel is essential for work, family and daily life. Excessive taxes increase living costs and push up the price of goods. We believe motorists deserve fairer prices, not endless taxation.",
        "background": "The UK Government should cap fuel tax using VAT at 20% but with no extra duties or hidden taxes on it. In the USA, petrol can cost the equivalent of around 84p per litre. We feel that British motorists deserve fairer prices, lower living costs and relief from excessive taxation.",
